    "case_id": "762",
    "case_summary": "A 32-year-old Chinese female with history of:- Born at 28 weeks by C-section for fetal distress- Antenatal period: reduced fetal movements and polyhydramnios- Very low birth weight (0.915 kg)- Delayed motor development in early childhood- At 16 years: progressive muscle weakness starting in lower limbs then upper limbs- By age 20: wheelchair-bound- At age 26: increasing shortness of breath and dysphagia- No significant family history of neuromuscular disorders\n\n- High-arched palate, elongated face with dolichocephaly- Muscle power (MRC scale):  * Proximal muscles: Grade 3- (upper limbs), Grade 2 (lower limbs)  * Distal muscles: Grade 3+ (both upper and lower limbs)- Normal deep tendon reflexes- Normal sensory examination- Normal cerebellar examination- Negative Tensilon test\n\nLaboratory Tests:- Mildly elevated plasma creatine kinase (379 U/L)- Normal thyroid function tests- Normal lactate and ammonia levels- Negative anti-acetylcholine receptor antibody- Normal plasma acylcarnitine and amino acids profile- Normal urine metabolic profiling- Normal acid alpha-glucosidase activityImaging:- Brain MRI (age 3): generalized cerebral atrophy and dilated ventricles- Brain CT (age 17): generalized cerebral atrophy, expanded sulcal spaces and ventricular systemElectrophysiological Studies:- Normal motor and sensory nerve conductions- Normal EMG at rest with no electrical myotonia- Giant motor unit potential and neuropathic changes in proximal and distal muscles- Long exercise test: 25% maximal decrement at 45 minutes post-exerciseMuscle Biopsy Findings:- H&E staining: fatty infiltration, mild fiber size variation, whorled fibers, internalized nuclei- NADH-TR staining: whorled fibers- Sudan black staining: scattered lipid droplets- Normal glycogen content on PAS staining- Preserved phosphofructokinase content",
